From 0b4c03b5ea22cc5fc16c074ccacfb3f0c8110c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter-Wijntjes <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:11:39 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: batch activation exports by request offset, never by
 lane order

Batched exports are sliced by request offset. That is the microbatch row
order whenever llama decodes the batch with split_simple, which is what a
unified KV cache does, and every multi-lane stage configures one. The old
admission additionally demanded consecutive lane ids in request order, a
condition the scheduler's FIFO batches almost never meet, so an exporting
stage silently executed every lane as its own graph.

Drop the ordering rule. A per-stream cache with more than one request, or a
batch that would not fit one microbatch on an exporting stage, is a contract
violation reported as an invalid argument; nothing in the batched path
signals "unsupported" any more.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp          |  4 ++
 src/llama-context.h            |  1 +
 src/skippy/execution-batch.cpp | 69 +++++++++++++++++-----------------
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

